{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/915868-supernatural-in-my-hunter-cell-yeah-another-thread","id":915868,"title":"Supernatural in my Hunter cell (yeah, another thread)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-16T15:14:59-07:00","id":915868,"title":"Supernatural in my Hunter cell (yeah, another thread)","content":"Preface: I know these threads pop up all the time. This one is specific to Changeling, which isn't particularly common in these threads and I know little about. <br /> <br /> So in my Hunter game, a new player brought a character concept to the table. He was explaining the concept to me and I told him &quot;That's pretty much exactly what changelings are.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. Can I still play him?&quot;<br /> <br /> So here I am. The character is a changeling who isn't really aware of other changelings in the area (read: I haven't written them in because I didn't expect them to come up) who is dedicated to hunting down Fae and their agents. <br /> <br /> I know next to nothing about Changeling. The game is 1e, and I don't know if the changeling character would upset the balance too much. I imagine he wouldn't use his abilities very often (to keep it a secret from other players/characters), but are there any pitfalls I should be concerned about with changelings?<br /> <br /> (Also, this will be a secret from other players as well, but I know my group and they'll be fine with it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2186-nerdynick","name":"Nerdynick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:35:30-07:00","id":915878,"title":"","content":"What books do you have access to? You say you're not really familiar with Changeling, which sends up a red flag in my view; I'd be inclined to grab <b>Mortal Remains</b> and to stat up this player's character as a Monster by combining the changeling-specific rules on pp.46\u201347 with the \u201cmonster template\u201d rules on pp.161\u2013165.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you go this route, I'd recommend reading <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players\">this topic</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-16-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:44:21-07:00","id":915887,"title":"","content":"The first thing you need to consider is that Changelings can see each other's Mein (true form) and the character would work best if their true form matched their mundane appearance, there is a Merit called &quot;No Seeming&quot; which is perfect for your needs.<br /> <br /> However I'd play it as if the player had the &quot;psychic ability&quot; to see monster's true forms, which is a valid interpretation of seeing other changeling's true forms.<br /> <br /> This would lead the Hunters to quickly identify many supernatural creatures, and set them up for the realization that many of them seem to not be hurting anyone and others are just terrible monsters if they do any thorough surveillance at all.<br /> <br /> Also things like horns, all black eyes, being made of fire or ice or wood or whatever, being covered with hair and fangs are all NORMAL Meins for changelings, as is Angelic beauty, and how &quot;nice&quot; they look is not really tied to how their behavior is.<br /> <br /> Also changeling's memory of their trauma while in Arcadia is intense but very hazy, but the desire to not be recaptured by what took them is powerful.<br /> <br /> If you want to avoid the balance issues try a mortal with the Fae Touched&quot; merit instead, you'd have all the &quot;seeing monsters everywhere!&quot; fun without the massive access to powers.<br /> <br /> Also don't forget changelings are often replaced with a Pod-Person type replacement called a Fetch to impersonate them while they are abducted by True Fae, and facing their own personal doppelganger that turns into a pile of bricker-brack upon being slain is terrifying without knowing the meaning of it all. It's pure paranoia-fuel if you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-16-2016, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:05:51-07:00","id":915929,"title":"","content":"In regards to books I have access to, I bought CtL on sale a while back to complete my collection, but I haven't really looked into it much. I have no other CtL books. <br /> <br /> In general, when introducing creatures in my game, I prefer not to use the Hunter systems (with dread powers and the like), but instead to use the native rules from their own game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2186-nerdynick","name":"Nerdynick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:49:28-07:00","id":915939,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>'s suggestion, mostly because I made a big guide to using Hunter for supernaturals in it, and now the idea is in my head and I wish I were able to run Hunter. Works best if you have Mortal Remains, though, since that has some Changeling focused Hunter stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}